# A folder that travels carries line endings with it, and a shell script with
# a carriage return in the shebang is dead on arrival:
#   /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
# That is what a Linux user got after copying this project across from Windows.
# Pin the shell scripts to LF everywhere, on every machine, and keep the .bat
# and .cmd twins on CRLF so Windows still runs them.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf

*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# The one Python file in the project: keep it CRLF, the way it is authored.
bonsai_web.py text eol=crlf

# Text that must never be rewritten, or a diff stops meaning anything.
*.gguf binary
*.onnx binary
*.wav binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.zip binary
*.tar.gz binary
